{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/touring-exhibition/881","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe, Imogen Cunningham, and Robert Mapplethorpe","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Oklahoma City Museum of Art (OKCMOA)","id":"actor/2047","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The exhibition is formed around OKCMOA’s Calla Lily (Lily – Yellow No. 2),1927 and presents a larger context for the work by showcasing a selection of O’Keeffe’s explorations of flowers in painting and photography. The exhibition discusses how the techniques of photography affected her paintings and demonstrate her changing approach to painting flowers over the course of her career.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"Activity"}